# Audio Player — waveform scrubber: a 22 s linear "playback" fills the 50 bars,
# the left pill shows the elapsed time (ReText from a worklet), and a pan on the
# waveform cancels playback, scrubs, then resumes from the finger's position.
# What this test covers: playback running on open; a tap in the middle
# (jump to ~0:11 and resume); a scrub right-to-left back to the start; a scrub
# past the right edge (clamped to 0:22, resume with a negative remaining time);
# a scrub past the left edge (x < 0); a diagonal scrub (the waveform pan must win
# over the app's pull-down close); rapid taps; and letting playback run to the end.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/audio-player"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait "text" "0:22" 30000
wait 2000
# Tap mid-waveform: jumps to ~0:11-0:13 and keeps playing.
press 191 462
wait 300
# Scrub right to left back to the start.
gesture pan 380 462 -350 0 800
wait 300
# Scrub past the right edge: clamps to the end; remaining time is negative.
gesture pan 30 462 370 0 700
wait 600
wait "value=\"0:22\"" 8000
# Scrub past the left edge (event.x < 0), then release.
gesture pan 200 462 -199 0 900
wait 1500
# Diagonal scrub with a downward component, inside the waveform.
gesture pan 100 450 200 50 600
wait 400
# (Elapsed-time text after a scrub is not asserted: under load a snapshot can
# take seconds while playback keeps running; the end state 0:22 is.)
# Rapid taps across the waveform.
press 60 462
wait 80
press 330 462
wait 80
press 120 462
wait 80
press 250 462
wait 80
press 40 462
wait 400
# Let playback run to the end (~22 s).
wait 23000
wait "value=\"0:22\"" 8000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
